    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0056" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12961</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-02">July 2, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Finland called to see me this afternoon and left with me the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> attached herewith.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d59-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I told the Minister that this Government, as well as the people of the United
                    States, continued to have the deepest interest in and sympathy for the people of
                    Finland in their struggle to maintain their independence and their liberty. I
                    said, however, that, for reasons which of course were obvious, this Government
                    would have to continue observing developments and that it would not at this time
                    be in a position to clarify its final attitude with regard to Finland beyond
                    that already indicated. I said that it was my most earnest hope that the
                    Government of Finland would not take any steps which would indicate an intention
                    on the part of Finland to permit the liberties for which the Finnish people have
                    so bravely fought to be now destroyed under the guise of German
                    “cooperation”.</p>
                <p>The Minister stated he was greatly concerned as to what the attitude of the
                    British Government would be towards Finland. I said I had as yet no definite
                    word with regard to that matter, but that I felt that for the time being the
                    attitude of the British Government was more or less the attitude of this
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
